      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is actually the override of the base class method that will get the \"appropriate\" dBm level for a given type. For LTE, the correct measurement of SignalStrength is Rsrp. In each of the CellSignalStrengthFoo() classes, there will be one specifically-named measurement that also maps to getDbm(). Since the meaning of this field is actually dependent on the underlying technology (same with ASU), it\u0027s debate-able whether this should have been put in the base class at all. Once the APIs merge to AOSP I think we should consider deprecating the getDbm() method for that reason... but that\u0027s for another day.",
